summary: Trash-bin: safely trash a file, or restore/prune (default: list)

!! Reference

```
Trash-bin: safely trash a file, or restore/prune (default: list)

Usage: mf trash [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  list     List the trashed files (id, size, age, reason, original path)
  restore  Restore a trashed file to its original path
  prune    Permanently delete trashed files (by size, age, or all)
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -f, --file <PATH>
          Move a tracked file into the trash (errors if it has no metarecord)

      --force
          Trash even when something outside still references its metarecords

  -h, --help
          Print help
```
